From 857b881733dd1236b52e4d55f3ccdc3616ae8cf8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 20:23:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] v2.9.9a: v3.0.0 security-gate remediation (4 findings from
 the adversarial review)

Fixes the four actionable findings from the v3.0.0-gate adversarial security
review of the v2.9.0..v2.9.9 window. All source-only, no blob work.

1. DNS Traffic Analyzer SQLi (inherited ASUS, compiled in under
   RTCONFIG_DNSQUERY_INTERCEPT): ej_dns_appStat / ej_dns_wanStat /
   ej_dns_wanStat_detail fed request params straight into
   dns_sqlite_Stat_hook() with no validation, unlike their sibling
   ej_dns_status, and their caller pages carry no Referer whitelist entry so
   the path is CSRF-rideable by a lured admin. New reaper_dns_stat_args_ok()
   mirrors ej_dns_status (MAC-or-empty client, enum-token mode, whitelisted
   dura, timestamp-or-empty date); out-of-spec input emits an empty array.

2. Restore upload parser overflow guard: do_reaper_restore_post used
   MIN(len+1, (int)sizeof(buf)) at six fgets sites - the (int) cast forces a
   signed compare, so a Content-Length near INT_MAX overflows len+1 to
   INT_MIN, wins the MIN, and passes a negative size to fgets. Stock and
   every other parser omit the cast. Dropped it (a v2.9.6 regression, CSRF-
   reachable, DoS-class).

3. sdn_rl template-literal breakout on Advanced_Smart_Connect.asp: the raw
   sdn_rl blob (which carries the user-set SDN network name) was embedded in
   a JS backtick literal, and nvram_get does not escape backtick/dollar-brace
   - a network named with a template expression executed in every admin
   session. Now read via the safe httpApi.nvramGet accessor the same file
   already uses.

4. CSV formula injection in the Devices export: a device/DHCP hostname is
   attacker-chosen; csvCell RFC-4180-quoted but did not neutralize a leading
   = + - @ / tab / CR. Prefix a single quote so the cell is text.

Latent findings from the same review were assessed and deliberately NOT
changed - each touches a regression-sensitive path (Tor IPv6 firewall
emission on a non-UI-reachable config; gatekeeper enforcement arming, whose
hold legitimately waits for a user-paced Complete-restore; first-boot
chpass) with benefit only on unreachable or admin-only paths. Documented for
the owner.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
